+  // draw that follows onFrameAvailable, and its queue silently drops a frame that a
+  // newer one replaces - no second onFrameAvailable. A scene that swaps early in
+  // every UI frame (the app's worklet globe) had every other frame thrown away: only
+  // 37-51% of the globe's rendered frames reached the screen. A setOpaque that
+  // changes the value is the one public call that marks the layer for update; done
+  // twice it changes nothing else. postOnAnimation, not post: it runs inside the
+  // next frame, before that frame's draw, where a plain post queued after the next
+  // vsync runs a frame late. Detached, the view would only queue them up.
+  // ponytail: rides on AOSP TextureView.setOpaque -> updateLayerAndInvalidate; a
+  // SurfaceView-backed GLView is the upgrade if a ROM ever stops doing that.
+  private val showLatest = Runnable { val o = isOpaque; isOpaque = !o; isOpaque = o }
